sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant H as Host/CPCI or ARM alias control
    participant P as input_arbiter + output_port_lookup
    participant F as convertible_fifo
    participant C as ARM CPU
    participant D as DMA
    participant G as GPU
    participant O as output_queues / egress

    H->>H: Hold CPU/GPU in reset; load IMEM and setup data
    H->>F: Set FIFO_MODE = 0
    P->>F: NF2 packet words {ctrl[7:0], data[63:0]}
    F-->>P: Deassert in_rdy after one count-delimited packet

    opt CPU packet/header preparation
        H->>F: Set FIFO_MODE = 1
        H->>C: Release CPU scheduler (CPU_CTRL.start_stop = 1)
        C->>F: 0x80-0xEF loads/stores map to FIFO[0x00-0x6F]
        C->>H: 0xF0-0xFF alias writes can configure DMA/GPU/FIFO
    end

    H->>F: Set FIFO_MODE = 2 and keep it stable
    H->>D: Program FIFO base, GPU base, length, dir=FIFO-to-GPU; pulse start
    D->>F: READ prime, then one 64-bit payload per COPY cycle
    D->>G: Write GPU DMEM Port B
    D-->>H: dma_active clears after N COPY cycles

    H->>G: Release GPU reset once to start at PC 0
    G->>G: IF -> ID -> EX1 -> EX2 -> EX3 -> WB inference
    G-->>H: kernel_done; wrapper freezes GPU cycle count

    H->>D: Program dir=GPU-to-FIFO; pulse start
    D->>G: Read GPU DMEM Port B
    D->>F: Write FIFO payload with ctrl=0
    D-->>H: dma_active clears

    H->>F: Return FIFO_MODE = 0 before drain
    H->>F: Pulse FIFO_DRAIN
    F->>O: Header + packet words, one per ready cycle
    Note over F,O: Current drain prefetch assumes continuous out_rdy; a stall can skip a word
    O-->>H: Response packet observed at selected egress

    Note over F,G: Port ownership summary: mode0 uses FIFO-B for drain; mode1+running uses CPU, otherwise PCI; mode2+active uses DMA on FIFO-B and GPU-DMEM-B, otherwise PCI
